{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"role based authorization role based authorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md","fileName":"Role-Based Authorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Role-Based Authorization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer]] [[Operating System Security and Access Control]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","Operating System Security and Access Control","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"role based authorization role based authorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md","fileName":"Role-Based Authorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Role-Based Authorization","heading":"Role-Based Authorization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Role-based authorization grants or denies an operation according to a role associated with the authenticated user. It allows two users who can both enter an application to receive different capabilities.\n\nThe stock checker separates read and update permissions so staff roles can expose only the operations each job requires. Server enforcement protects the API, while matching UI changes avoid presenting controls that the current user cannot successfully invoke.\n\nIn an operating-system security model, role-based control groups permissions by user category, such as a general user or administrator. Changing the role changes the available operations without requiring an independent rule for every user-resource pair.","tags":["baby"],"links":["OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","Operating System Security and Access Control","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"role based authorization role based authorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Role-Based Authorization.md","fileName":"Role-Based Authorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Role-Based Authorization","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[cybersecurity.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","Operating System Security and Access Control","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}